# Full pipeline default

After changes to **`analysis/`**, **`medevac_report.qmd`**, or **`scripts/run_full_pipeline.py`**, run the full pipeline so tables, figures, and HTML stay in sync:

```bash
# Local / de-identified data + village codebook:
python3 scripts/run_full_pipeline.py -synthetic

# PHI / real community names (omit -synthetic):
python3 scripts/run_full_pipeline.py
```

**Outputs to review:** `_quarto_output/medevac_report.html` (open in browser), plus `outputs/tables/*.csv` and `outputs/figures/*.png`.

**Do not commit** `outputs/figures/` or `outputs/data/` — they are gitignored and regenerated locally (synthetic vs PHI). Never use `git add -f` on pipeline PNGs.

When the user asks to “see the data” or refresh the report, prefer this command unless they specify otherwise.
